  "body": "Admittedly, most link relations do not actually impact browsers, so this removal doesn't seem urgent. But it seems to me like sidebar once upon a time meant something (in Netscape and SeaMonkey), and was never implemented elsewhere. And, unlike rels like alternate or license or next, there isn't much semantic value in sidebar for non-browser user agents:\n\n> The sidebar keyword indicates that the referenced document, if retrieved, is intended to be shown in a secondary browsing context (if possible), instead of in the current browsing context.\n\nI know Firefox does still have a sidebar, but I wasn't able to get any documents to display in it.\n\nDoes anyone object to removing this?\n",
